run-gpu-team-loops.m's solver spawned on the machine's GPU, its distribute
loops across the teams of its module's kernel and its parallel do loops
across each team's threads, which prints what it prints at the host, the
output the oracle checked. Without -fopenmp the directives are comments,
and the solver runs its loops itself.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/run-gpu-team-loops.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %S/run-gpu-team-loops.m --check-prefix=OUTPUT --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/run-gpu-team-loops.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t.sequential gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %S/run-gpu-team-loops.m --check-prefix=OUTPUT --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
